wsi/metal: offer every colour space without VK_EXT_swapchain_colorspace

wsi_metal_surface_get_formats and get_formats2 only list sRGB unless the application enabled
VK_EXT_swapchain_colorspace. vkd3d-proton never enables it, so a D3D12 game's HDR10 swapchain
(DXGI_COLOR_SPACE_RGB_FULL_G2084_NONE_P2020) was refused and Forza Horizon 6 stayed in SDR with HDR on.
Offer the full list, as other WSI backends effectively do. Pairs with 0008.

Tested in Forza Horizon 6 on a base M5 (macOS 27.2), applied to the r2 driver as a binary patch with 0008:
the swapchain is created with VK_COLOR_SPACE_HDR10_ST2084_EXT, the layer gets kCGColorSpaceITUR_2100_PQ
with wantsExtendedDynamicRangeContent, and the game shows HDR. In windowed mode it gets the display's full
EDR headroom. In full screen, macOS gave it about 1.0x headroom, which looks like a separate macOS-side
limit (possibly Game Mode), not this patch.

--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal.c
@@ -251,10 +251,9 @@
 
    VkFormat sorted_formats[ARRAY_SIZE(available_surface_formats)];
    get_sorted_vk_formats(wsi_device->force_bgra8_unorm_first, sorted_formats);
-   unsigned color_space_count =
-      pdev->instance->enabled_extensions.EXT_swapchain_colorspace
-         ? ARRAY_SIZE(available_surface_color_spaces)
-         : 1u;
+   /* Offer every colour space even when the application did not enable VK_EXT_swapchain_colorspace:
+    * vkd3d-proton never enables it, so HDR10 was hidden and DXGI HDR swapchains stayed sRGB. */
+   unsigned color_space_count = ARRAY_SIZE(available_surface_color_spaces);
 
    for (unsigned i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sorted_formats); i++) {
       for (unsigned j = 0; j < color_space_count; j++) {
@@ -280,10 +279,9 @@
 
